    "body": "## Summary\n\nAllow HiCache host-memory sizing to fall back to the process cgroup limit when the process is inside a namespaced cgroup path that is not mirrored under `/sys/fs/cgroup`.\n\nPyxis/Enroot can expose a path such as `/slurm/...` in `/proc/self/cgroup` while mounting the allocation's cgroup directory as the container's cgroup root. In that case the existing joined path does not exist even though `/sys/fs/cgroup/memory.max` contains the correct limit.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Added unit coverage for the namespaced-path fallback.\n- Ran the HiCache unit test.\n- Ran Dynamo's two-worker HiCache launch flow end to end under Pyxis on H100 NVL; both workers started and a real chat-completion request returned HTTP 200.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40994130009](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40994130009)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40994129788](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40994129788)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40994129908](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40994129908)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
